!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = T-ALL Cell line
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: CUTLL1
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = disease state: T-ALL
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = chip antibody: H3K27ac (Active motif; Catalog no: 39133)
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = N/A
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = CUTLL1 cells were grown in RPMI medium with 10% FBS
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Nuclear extraction and DNA purification using Amicon Ultra 30K
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Libraries prepared using Kapa Hper Library prep kits (KK8504) as per manufacturer's guidelines.
!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: HiChIP
!Sample_data_processing = Read alignment: bowtie2 2.2.3. Paired-end reads were mapped against the mm10 reference sequence using bowtie2 (special paramters: --very-sensitive-local --local)
!Sample_data_processing = Filtering: GenomicTools "gtools-hic filter". Discards read-pairs marked as multihits, only one mappable read, positional duplicates, low mapping quality (MAPQ < 20), self-ligated fragments, short-range interactions (<10 kb)
!Sample_data_processing = Matrix generation: HicBench. For each replicate and each chromosome, a matrix with binned interactions (bin-size 10kb) was generated.
!Sample_data_processing = Normalization: custom script. Each loop with > 1 read was kept. We applied normalization by sequencing depth to raw read-counts (leading to counts-per-million; CPM).
!Sample_data_processing = High-confidence interactions: custom script. We have applied an approach similar to mango, which employs a binomial test per diagnoal in the normalized counts-matrix. To define significant HiChIP loops, we have filtered all interactions for CPM>5 and FDR<0.1.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: hg19
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: TSV - significant loops
